{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"Issue #295 requires operator launch recipes, secret handling, explicit agent-owned-tool and Timeline guidance, an opt-in live smoke path outside CI, and live evidence or per-agent blockers after its five implementation prerequisites landed.","decision":"Document opencode, Codex, and Claude Agent launch/auth recipes and package limitations; add a standalone one-Turn live smoke executable with interactive permission decisions and an isolated temporary working directory; expose it through a Make target not referenced by verify; record redacted per-agent outcomes on #295.","impact":"README and backend operator guide now describe secrets, Timeline/session mapping, cancellation, and agent-owned tools. The Swift package builds the smoke executable, while verify only builds it and never runs a live agent. Live OpenCode and Codex Turns passed; Claude Agent reached permission mediation and failed closed because its allow_always/allow/reject option set is unsupported. No credential values or fixtures were added. make docs-check and make verify passed before the final target/cache issue; the latest documentation checker and git diff --check passed. A later package rebuild was blocked by Git dubious-ownership errors in the shared SwiftPM cache.","recurrence_control":"Keep make acp-live-smoke as an explicit operator target with an agent selector and bounded runtime; keep it out of verify/CI. Maintain per-agent transcripts and replacement conditions on issue #295, and re-run the Claude smoke when the permission option contract is supported.","rejected_alternatives":["Adding live agents to make verify or CI, which would make test outcomes depend on user credentials and network services.","Putting credentials in fixtures or tracked configuration."],"sources":[]}
